    "updated_at": "2026-06-01T10:27:11Z",
    "body": "I'm not quite sure I understand the current definition\n\"When the API is successfully used, the API is enabled for use by all [descendant navigables](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#descendant-navigables) of the [top-level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-top)’s [active document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-document) (that is, all frames on the current page) can access the API without further availability checks.\"\n\n\"Each activation makes the API available to at most one site.\"\n\nSo if top  level page has cross-site iframes, what is the expected behavior in those iframes?\nBut perhaps I get confused with \"available\" and \"enabled\" here?",
